# CMake build output. `build-*` as well as `build/`: run-checks.sh puts each
# sanitizer and the clang lane in its own tree beside it, and without the glob
# they were committed -- 534 object files carrying one machine's absolute paths,
# which then made every sanitizer lane fail to configure anywhere else.
build/
build-*/
_CPack_Packages/

# Packaged artifacts. The release driver stages the .deb and its detached
# signatures and checksum in the repo root before uploading them to the GitHub
# release, and `release.sh --publish` runs `git add -A` -- without these an
# 11 MB package would be committed on every release. The exported PUBLIC signing
# key (micronotes-signing-key.asc) is deliberately NOT matched: it is tracked,
# because a user verifying a download needs it from somewhere they can trust.
*.deb
/micronotes_*_amd64.deb.asc
/micronotes_*_amd64.deb.sha256
/micronotes_*_amd64.deb.sha256.asc

# Agent worktrees. `session-compare.sh` and the parity work both build a
# baseline in a git worktree under here; a worktree's `.git` file makes it look
# like an embedded repository, and `git add -A` will happily track it as a
# gitlink pointing at a path that exists on one machine.
.claude/worktrees/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
